# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
# WQ_EMAIL / WQ_PASSWORD. .env.example is the tracked template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ------------------------------------------------------------ runtime data
# EVERYTHING under data/ is ignored by default, deliberately.
#
# Nothing in there belongs in version control, and the three reasons overlap:
#
#   secret        cookies.json is a live BRAIN session (mode 600);
#                 persona_url.txt and auth_wait.log carry persona inquiry URLs
#                 and the account's BRAIN user id; and EVERY *.log line like
#                 "reusing persisted session for <you>@example.com" leaks the
#                 account email. Logs here are a credential leak, not noise.
#
#   local state   machine.db is this machine's memory -- 1,500+ candidates,
#                 sims, in-flight slots. biometric_attempts.json is a rolling
#                 24h quota counter that is only meaningful on this host.
#
#   regenerable   data/cache/fields_*.json is ~49 MB of catalog that `catalog`
#                 rebuilds on demand.
#
# Deny-by-default rather than an enumerated list: new logs, caches and sidecar
# files appear here constantly, and the failure mode of forgetting one is
# committing a session cookie. Every writer calls makedirs(exist_ok=True), so
# the directory rebuilds itself on a fresh clone -- nothing needs tracking to
# keep the layout.
data/*

# If you ever want the LLM dataset priors in the repo, this is the one file
# worth the argument: ~$0.70 of claude-sonnet-5 calls, account-independent, and
# a fresh clone otherwise re-pays for it. Re-including it needs the whole path
# chain unignored, so it is left commented rather than half-done:
#   !data/cache/
#   data/cache/*
#   !data/cache/arm_priors.json

# ------------------------------------------------- databases (also outside data/)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

